        "content": "Read one document and report what it says in answer to a question. Use only this document: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no guesses.\n\nQuestion: When was the Elks organization founded?\n\nDocument:\nImproved Benevolent and Protective Order of Elks of the World The Improved Benevolent Protective Order of Elks of the World or IBPOEW is an African-American fraternal order modeled on the Benevolent and Protective Order of Elks. It was established in 1897. In the early 21st century, with 500,000 members and 1500 lodges in the world, the IBPOEW claims to be the largest black fraternal organization. The Order claims descent from the Free African Society, the first formal black society in America, founded in 1787 as a mutual aid society by Absalom Jones and Richard Allen in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. Its formal\n\nReply with JSON only, in this form:\n{\"relevant\": true, \"cards\": [{\"entity\": \"\", \"sense\": \"\", \"answer\": \"\", \"as_of\": \"\", \"claim_kind\": \"\", \"attributed_to\": \"\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"claim\": \"\"}]}\n\n\"relevant\": false if the document is about some other topic and is of no use for the question; then \"cards\" is [].\n\"cards\": one card for each answer the document itself gives to the question. Usually that is one card. It is several cards if the document gives several answers, such as a list of names: one card each. It is [] if the document gives no answer. The question may fit several things that share a name: whichever of them this document is about, report its answer. If the document only says that some answer is wrong, write no card for that answer.\n\nThe fields of a card:\n- \"entity\": who or what this answer is about, as specifically as the document identifies it: the full name, plus the details the document gives that tell it apart from others with the same name (what kind of thing it is, profession or role, nationality or place, years, creator, other names), even where the question does not ask